module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ExceptionalProjectiveLine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ExceptionalTwistSequence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjectiveSpaceEmbeddingTwist

/-!
# The twists of the exceptional divisor are the twists of projective space

Let `R` be a commutative ring, `I ⊆ R` an ideal generated by `m` elements and
`X = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` the blowup of `Spec R` in `I`, with exceptional divisor `E` and inclusion
`i : E ⟶ X`. Suppose `E` has been identified with the special fibre
`𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I} = Proj (R/I)[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]` by an isomorphism `ρ` through which the closed
immersion `r : X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` restricted to `E` factors — the datum part (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] produces. Then

`i^* 𝒪_X(n) ≅ ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)` for every `n : ℤ`,

that is, the restriction to `E` of the `n`-th twist of the blowup is, under the identification
`ρ`, the `n`-th Serre twist on projective space over `R/I`. For `R = A` a two-dimensional regular
local ring and `I = 𝔪` this is the sentence of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] that reads "by
Lemma 0AGQ we have `E = 𝐏¹_κ` *and* `𝒪_E(1)` indeed corresponds to the usual Serre twist of the
structure sheaf on `𝐏¹`": part (1) of Tag 0AGQ supplies `E = 𝐏¹_κ` and nothing more, and this
file supplies the second half, which is what makes `H⁰(E, 𝒪_E(n-1))` and `H¹(E, 𝒪_E(n-1))`
computable by Serre's calculation on the projective line.

## The route

Three facts already in the library compose, and nothing else is needed:

* part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ], `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso`:
  `r^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(n) ≅ 𝒪_X(n)`, so `i^*𝒪_X(n) ≅ i^*r^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(n) = (i ≫ r)^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(n)`;
* the factorization `i ≫ r = ρ ≫ (𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I} ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R})`, which is the compatibility
  clause of part (1) of the tag
  (`Stacks.Blowup.subschemeι_comp_blowUpSpecToProjSpace`), so that
  `(i ≫ r)^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(n) = ρ^*(𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I} ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R})^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}}(n)`;
* part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 01N1], `ProjMapTwistDegreeSection.pullbackTwistIso`, at the
  coefficient-change homomorphism `R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] ⟶ (R/I)[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]`, which is
  surjective with source generated in degree one: the inclusion of the special fibre pulls
  `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}}(n)` back to `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.restrictionPullbackTwistIso`: `(r|_E)^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}}(n) ≅
  ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`, for any `ρ` satisfying the factorization.
* `Stacks.Blowup.pullbackExceptionalTwistIso`: **`i^* 𝒪_X(n) ≅ ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`**, for
  any `ρ` satisfying the factorization.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_conormalSheaf_iso_pullback_specialFibreTwist_one` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_normalSheaf_iso_pullback_specialFibreTwist_neg_one`:
  `𝒞_{E/X} ≅ ρ^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(1)` and `𝒩_{E/X} ≅ ρ^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(-1)`, the form of
  part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] in which `r|_E` is read as the morphism `ρ` to the special fibre.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_iso_exceptional_projectiveLine_pullbackTwist`: the same for the blowup of
  a two-dimensional regular local ring in its maximal ideal and any generating pair of `𝔪`, with
  `ρ` produced by part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] and the factorization discharged — the
  identification `E = 𝐏¹_κ` *together with* the identification of every `𝒪_E(n)` with the Serre
  twist `𝒪_{𝐏¹_κ}(n)`.

## Implementation notes

**No `stacks` attribute is attached.** The twist comparison along `i` is not an assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 0AGQ]: part (1) of that tag asserts the isomorphism `E ≅ 𝐏¹_κ` and the
factorization of `r|_E` through it, and parts (2) and (3) are statements about `X` and about the
conormal and normal sheaves of `E`. The remark that `𝒪_E(1)` corresponds to the Serre twist is
made inside the *proof* of [Stacks, Tag 0AGS], where it is used; it is registered nowhere.

The comparison is assembled from `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr`; the latter is how the factorization of `r|_E`
enters, an equality of morphisms of schemes turning into an isomorphism of pullback functors.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf)

universe u

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

namespace Stacks.Blowup

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)

/-- **The inclusion of the special fibre pulls `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}}(n)` back to
`𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`.** This is part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 01N1] at the coefficient-change
homomorphism `R[T₀, …, T_{m-1}] ⟶ (R/I)[T₀, …, T_{m-1}]`, which is surjective because
`R ⟶ R/I` is, and whose source is generated in degree one over its degree-zero part. -/
def specialFibrePullbackTwistIso (m : ℕ) (n : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
            (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
              (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) n) ≅
      twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)) n :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjMapTwistDegreeSection.pullbackTwistIso
    (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) _
    (MvPolynomial.map_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective)
    (MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top (Fin m) R) n

/-- **Pulling a twist of `𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` back along `r|_E` is pulling the Serre twist of
`𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}` back along `ρ`.** Let `ρ : E ≅ 𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}` be an isomorphism of the
exceptional divisor onto the special fibre through which the restriction
`r|_E : E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` factors. Then

`(r|_E)^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}}(n) ≅ ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`

for every `n : ℤ`: the factorization turns `(r|_E)^*` into `ρ^*` composed with the pullback along
the inclusion of the special fibre, which is `Stacks.Blowup.specialFibrePullbackTwistIso`. -/
def restrictionPullbackTwistIso {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (ρ : (exceptionalIdealData I).subscheme ≅
      Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)))
    (hcomp : (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan =
      ρ.hom ≫ Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
        (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (n : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          ((exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) R) n) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)) n) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr hcomp).app _ ≪≫
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp ρ.hom
      (Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
        (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))).app _).symm ≪≫
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).mapIso (specialFibrePullbackTwistIso I m n)

/-- **The conormal sheaf of the exceptional divisor is `ρ^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(1)`.** For an
isomorphism `ρ : E ≅ 𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}` onto the special fibre through which the restriction
`r|_E : E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of the closed immersion attached to `x` factors, the conormal
sheaf `𝒞_{E/X}` is the pullback along `ρ` of the Serre twist `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(1)`. -/
theorem nonempty_conormalSheaf_iso_pullback_specialFibreTwist_one {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (ρ : (exceptionalIdealData I).subscheme ≅
      Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)))
    (hcomp : (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan =
      ρ.hom ≫ Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
        (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)) 1)) := by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_conormalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_one I x hx hspan
  exact ⟨e ≪≫ restrictionPullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan ρ hcomp 1⟩

/-- **The normal sheaf of the exceptional divisor is `ρ^*𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(-1)`.** For an
isomorphism `ρ : E ≅ 𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}` onto the special fibre through which the restriction
`r|_E : E ⟶ X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}` of the closed immersion attached to `x` factors, the normal
sheaf `𝒩_{E/X}` is the pullback along `ρ` of the Serre twist `𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(-1)`. -/
theorem nonempty_normalSheaf_iso_pullback_specialFibreTwist_neg_one {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I) (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (ρ : (exceptionalIdealData I).subscheme ≅
      Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)))
    (hcomp : (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan =
      ρ.hom ≫ Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
        (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))) :
    Nonempty (Stacks.Divisors.normalSheaf (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)) (-1))) := by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_normalSheaf_iso_pullback_twistingSheaf_neg_one I x hx hspan
  exact ⟨e ≪≫ restrictionPullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan ρ hcomp (-1)⟩

/-- **The twists of the exceptional divisor are the twists of projective space.** Let
`X = Proj (⨁ₙ Iⁿ)` be the blowup of `Spec R` in an ideal `I` generated by `x₀, …, x_{m-1}`, with
exceptional divisor `E`, inclusion `i : E ⟶ X` and closed immersion
`r : X ⟶ 𝐏^{m-1}_{Spec R}`. Let `ρ : E ≅ 𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}` be an isomorphism onto the special fibre
through which `r|_E` factors. Then

`i^* 𝒪_X(n) ≅ ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏^{m-1}_{R/I}}(n)`

for every `n : ℤ`: restricting the `n`-th twist of the blowup to the exceptional divisor gives,
under `ρ`, the `n`-th Serre twist on projective space over `R/I`.

The hypothesis `hcomp` is the compatibility clause of part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ]; for the
maximal ideal of a two-dimensional regular local ring it is discharged in
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_iso_exceptional_projectiveLine_pullbackTwist`. -/
def pullbackExceptionalTwistIso {m : ℕ} (x : Fin m → R) (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ I)
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (ρ : (exceptionalIdealData I).subscheme ≅
      Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)))
    (hcomp : (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι ≫ blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan =
      ρ.hom ≫ Proj.map (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
        (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin m)
          (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (n : ℤ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι).obj (blowUpTwist I n) ≅
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).obj
        (twistingSheaf (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin m) (R ⧸ I)) n) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι).mapIso
      (blowUpSpecToProjSpacePullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan n).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp (exceptionalIdealData I).subschemeι
        (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).app _ ≪≫
      restrictionPullbackTwistIso I x hx hspan ρ hcomp n

open IsLocalRing in
/-- **The exceptional divisor of the blowup of a regular local surface is `𝐏¹_κ` with its Serre
twists.** Let `(A, 𝔪, κ)` be a regular local ring of dimension two, `X = Proj (⨁ₙ 𝔪ⁿ)` the
blowup of `Spec A` in `𝔪` and `E` its exceptional divisor. For every generating pair `x` of `𝔪`
there is an isomorphism `ρ : E ≅ 𝐏¹_κ` through which the restriction to `E` of the closed
immersion `r : X ⟶ 𝐏¹_{Spec A}` attached to `x` factors — part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0AGQ] — and,
in addition, for every `n : ℤ`

`i^* 𝒪_X(n) ≅ ρ^* 𝒪_{𝐏¹_κ}(n)`,

so that the restriction of every twist of the blowup to the exceptional divisor is the
corresponding Serre twist on the projective line over the residue field. -/
theorem exists_iso_exceptional_projectiveLine_pullbackTwist (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    [IsRegularLocalRing A] (hdim : ringKrullDim A = 2) (x : Fin 2 → A)
    (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ maximalIdeal A) (hspan : maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span (Set.range x)) :
    ∃ ρ : (exceptionalIdealData (maximalIdeal A)).subscheme ≅
        Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) (A ⧸ maximalIdeal A)),
      (exceptionalIdealData (maximalIdeal A)).subschemeι ≫
          blowUpSpecToProjSpace (maximalIdeal A) x hx hspan =
        ρ.hom ≫ Proj.map
          (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.polyGradedMap (Fin 2)
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal A)))
          (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.irrelevant_le_map_polyGradedMap (Fin 2)
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal A))) ∧
      ∀ n : ℤ, Nonempty
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback
              (exceptionalIdealData (maximalIdeal A)).subschemeι).obj
            (blowUpTwist (maximalIdeal A) n) ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ρ.hom).obj
            (twistingSheaf
              (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) (A ⧸ maximalIdeal A)) n)) := by
  obtain ⟨ρ, hcomp⟩ := exists_iso_exceptional_projectiveLine A hdim x hx hspan
  exact ⟨ρ, hcomp, fun n => ⟨pullbackExceptionalTwistIso _ x hx hspan ρ hcomp n⟩⟩

end Stacks.Blowup

end
